#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:21
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <acronym>print</acronym> KIOSlave gives quick access to browse different "
"&kdeprint; sections via <quote>virtual folders</quote>. These folders "
"provide some information about and quick access to your print subsystem."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:26
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<command>print:/</command> represents one more of those useful KIOSlaves "
"implemented by &kde;. To access it, just type <userinput>print:/ </"
"userinput> into the address field of &konqueror;. <userinput>print:/ </"
"userinput> doesn't purely provide <quote>read-only</quote> access to your "
"print subsystem, but it also allows you to change settings of your printers, "
"of your print system and lets you create new printers and classes."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:34
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You are asked for the Administrator or root password, if you are not allowed "
"a view or an operation as a normal user."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:37
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can bookmark frequently used shortcuts like <command>print:/manager</"
"command>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:40
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Valid syntax is either <userinput>print:/[path-to-virtual-folder]</"
"userinput> or <userinput>print:[path-to-virtual-folder]</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:44
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Note, that some of the views and actions offered do heavily depend on the "
"print subsystem that is installed on your box and presently activated for "
"&kde;. Pages showing printer information display only those parts that are "
"valid for the &kde; selected print subsystem. (So if you normally run "
"<acronym>CUPS</acronym>, but switched temporarily to <quote>Generic UNIX LPD "
"Printing</quote>, which is possible, you will see less printer info, because "
"LPD is not capable of using the same amount of print settings as are "
"possible in CUPS)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:55
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Valid syntax to access different virtual folders and a short explanation of "
"what they represent:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:59
#, no-c-format
msgid "Some examples"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:62
#, no-c-format
msgid "<userinput>print:/ </userinput> (&ie; the root of print-kioslave)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:65
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"virtual root for browsing your print subsystem. It displays subfolders "
"<quote>Classes</quote>, <quote>Jobs</quote>, <quote>Manager</quote>, "
"<quote>Printers</quote>, and <quote>Specials</quote>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:74
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput>print:/classes</userinput> or <userinput>print:classes </"
"userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:77
#, no-c-format
msgid "view your printer classes (supported by and useful for CUPS only)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:85
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput>print:/classes/class_name </userinput> or <userinput>print:"
"classes/class_name </userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:87
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"view all members of the named printer class (supported by and useful only "
"for CUPS)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:95
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput>print:/jobs </userinput> or <userinput>print:jobs </userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:98
#, no-c-format
msgid "lists the current and pending jobs."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:103
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput>print:/printers </userinput> or <userinput>print:printers </"
"userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:106
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"lists all your printers. Clicking on a printer name shows more info about "
"that printer."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:113
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput>print:/printers/printer_name </userinput> or <userinput>print:"
"printers/printer_name </userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:116
#, no-c-format
msgid "displays useful info about the named printer"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:122
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput>print:/manager </userinput> or <userinput>print:manager </"
"userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:125
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"opens a page very similar to the &kdeprint; Manager module inside the &kde; "
"Control Center. Switch to a different printing system here or do every other "
"administrative task."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:129
#, no-c-format
msgid "This is the most important of access points to your printing system."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:135
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput>print:/specials </userinput> or <userinput>print:specials </"
"userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:138
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"lists all presently available <quote>special printers</quote>: Likely you'll "
"see:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:142
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The two that let you save a printfile to disk, in &PostScript; or "
"<acronym>PDF</acronym> format."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:146
#, no-c-format
msgid "One that sends it as a <acronym>PDF</acronym> attachment via &kmail;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:150
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"And last, send it via fax, if you have one of the supported fax backends "
"active, <application>Hylafax</application> or <application>efax</"
"application>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:161
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can also put <command>print:/manager</command> or similar as the command "
"in the <quote>Quick Command</quote> utility (started via <keycombo action="
"\"simul\">&Alt;<keycap>F2</keycap></keycombo>)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:166
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can learn more about printing and &kdeprint;'s powerful abilities by "
"reading the <ulink url=\"help:/kdeprint/index.html\">&kdeprint; Handbook "
"locally</ulink> or at the <ulink url=\"http://printing.kde.org/\">&kdeprint; "
"Website</ulink> where there are documents online (<acronym>HTML</acronym> "
"and <acronym>PDF</acronym>),containing <ulink url=\"http://printing.kde.org/"
"documentation/tutorials/\">Tutorials</ulink>, as well as <ulink url=\"http://"
"printing.kde.org/faq/\">FAQs</ulink> and Tips and Tricks related to printing "
"in general."
msgstr ""
